tools.description:
Read-only, one row per person across this page's teams: members, pending team invitations, people invited to Spaces, and SSO identity grants. Enterprise and Internal plans only. Covers only scope.teams and the Spaces this credential can read; getTeamExternalAccessSummary reports whether permissions hide anything. A person's other verified addresses, and an identity grant's subject and issuer, are never returned. Links, passwords, public access, team-audience grants and the parent-team grant are not people and are excluded. scope.companyDomains and emailDomain report join rules, which offer joining and do not restrict sign-in or invitations.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamExternalAccessPeople(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// `outside` keeps people with no verified address at a company domain. Answers company_domains_unavailable when scope.companyDomains is null, and a validation error when it is empty, never an empty list.
emailDomain?: "all" | "outside", // default: "all"
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// People in this team, or holding access to a Space in it. A team outside scope.teams is not found.
owningTeamId?: string, // minLength: 1
// Matches the name or email shown on a row, an address the person was invited at, or an SSO identity's name.
q?: string, // maxLength: 200
// `members` holds an active membership in scope, `invited` a pending team invitation in scope (the two can overlap), and `guests` neither, with access to at least one Space. With owningTeamId, each looks at that team alone.
show?: "all" | "members" | "invited" | "guests", // default: "all"
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Paginated connector names and active team-owned account counts, ordered by connector name. The owning team must be in this page's scope (otherwise not found), and the credential needs connector read permission and eligibility for it. Enterprise and Internal plans only. Personal, visitor and revoked accounts, credentials and private connection identities are excluded. Does not verify provider health or data flow.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamExternalAccessTeamConnectors(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
owningTeamId: string, // minLength: 1
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Paginated settings for the teams in this page's scope that the credential can read, ordered by team name and ID. Enterprise and Internal plans only. Connector reads respect credential permissions. Returns up to three configured team-account connector names per team; follow each connector cursor with listTeamExternalAccessTeamConnectors. No credentials, private account identities or provider requests.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamExternalAccessTeams(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's live spaces that nobody published or changed in the given number of days, least recently active first. Pinned and archived spaces are not included. Only team owners and admins can use this operation.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamInactiveSpaces(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Return Spaces with no publish or change in this number of days. The default is 90.
days?: integer, // default: 90, minimum: 1, maximum: 3650
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's invitations and their statuses, newest-first.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamInvitations(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// The team whose invitations to list.
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns every label the team has, ordered by name.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamLabels(args: {
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns every feature a team can join before it is generally available, with its stage, how a team joins, the team's enrollment, and whether the team has the feature now. `enabled` is the team's real answer: an emergency stop or a missing plan entitlement can keep a feature off while its enrollment is active.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamLabs(args: {
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's members with their roles, newest-first.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamMembers(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Lists pending, unexpired membership requests for a subteam's administrator. A key or agent approved on the parent team with member-write can read them too.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamMembershipRequests(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Counts and lists the members of the root team and its subteams whose primary address is outside the verified domains, so no SSO sign-in reaches them while the team requires SSO. Names any verified secondary address on a verified domain, which the member can make primary to use SSO. Also counts them by their address's domain, each with the pending domain that would cover it once verified. Needs a team owner or admin.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamMemberSignInBlocked(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's active memories, all on one page, or with `status=archived` the archived ones, most recently archived first and paged by `limit` and `cursor`: pass the previous page's `pagination.nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false. Each memory says who saved and last edited it. Pass `spaceId` to keep team-wide memories and that Space's memories only. Use this to manage memories; before starting work, read `getTeamAgentContext` instead.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamMemories(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Only team-wide memories and memories about this Space.
spaceId?: string, // pattern: /^(spc_)[A-Za-z0-9]+$/
// Active memories (the default), all on one page, or archived ones, paged by `limit` and `cursor`.
status?: "active" | "archived", // default: "active"
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Lists the team's OAuth clients (Sign in with Spacefast apps and machine clients), newest first. Filter by `profile` (`connect_app` or `machine`). Client secrets are never returned here.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamOAuthClients(args: {
profile?: "connect_app" | "machine",
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the teams your credential can act for, newest-first. With `deleted=true`, returns only the teams this credential's user deleted.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeams(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Set true to list only the teams you deleted, newest first. Nobody else sees a deleted team, teammates included.
deleted?: boolean | ("true" | "false"),
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns every preset team skill, such as SEO or Spam protection, with its instructions and whether it is on for this team. `setup` names a secret team variable the skill needs, and `configured` says whether the team saved it. The variable's value is never returned.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamSkills(args: {
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Lists pending, verified Space requests across this team's live Spaces, newest first. Requires member administration permission.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamSpaceAccessRequests(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's live spaces, most recently updated first. With `archived=true`, returns its archived spaces instead.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamSpaces(args: {
// Return the team's archived spaces instead of its live ones. Restore one with POST /v1/spaces/{spaceId}/restore.
archived?: string,
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Lists draft, review, approved, released, and abandoned tag revisions for the team.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamTagRevisions(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Return only revisions in this review state.
status?: "draft" | "in_review" | "approved" | "publishing" | "published" | "abandoned",
teamId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the team's variables. Secret values are never returned; secrets expose only their metadata.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listTeamVariables(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Every budget on the team, its subteams and its Spaces, with this period's usage against it. A plan's built-in budget (Free's included usage) is listed with `system: true`.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listUsageBudgets(args: {
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Returns the webhook's delivery attempts with statuses and diagnostics, newest-first.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listWebhookDeliveries(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
webhookId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Lists the webhooks on teams that your credential can read, newest first. A tenant-rooted credential also sees the tenant's own subscriptions, declared in its system-space manifest.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__listWebhooks(args: {
// Opaque cursor from the previous page's `nextCursor`.
cursor?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 4096
// Page size.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Filter to one team's webhooks, by team id or slug. Leaves out tenant-owned subscriptions. A team the credential cannot reach answers 404.
teamId?: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Makes Spaces in the teams this page covers private and closes their link and password access: revokes every managed public grant, scheduled ones included, every share link and every password, and turns search indexing off. Any member of an Enterprise or Internal team can call it; each Space also requires Space write access and access management on it. Each Space succeeds or fails on its own, and repeating the call revokes nothing new. Public access declared in sf.jsonc stays until the source changes and is published (needs_publish). Team members, invited people and connectors are unchanged. Revoked links and passwords cannot be restored.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__lockDownTeamExternalAccess(args: {
body: {
// Spaces in the parent's current family to lock down.
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 100
spaceIds: Array<
string // minLength: 1
>,
},
teamId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Marks a comment thread read for you.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__markSpaceCommentRead(args: {
spaceId: string, // minLength: 1
threadId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Merge branches in a hosted repository. Send expectedTargetSha to reject changes if the target branch moved. A merge does not confirm deployment.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__mergeSpaceSourceBranches(args: {
body: {
allowUnrelatedHistories?: boolean,
// Git author. Omit it to use the registered profile of the authenticated user or machine credential creator. Attribution does not change permissions.
author?: {
email: string, // pattern: /^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_'+\-]+\.)*[A-Za-z0-9_'+\-]*[A-Za-z0-9_+-]@(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\-]*\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$/, format: "email"
name: string, // minLength: 1
},
commitMessage?: string, // minLength: 1
committer?: {
email: string, // pattern: /^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_'+\-]+\.)*[A-Za-z0-9_'+\-]*[A-Za-z0-9_+-]@(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\-]*\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$/, format: "email"
name: string, // minLength: 1
},
connectionType: "connected" | "hosted",
expectedTargetSha?: string, // minLength: 1
sourceBranch: string, // minLength: 1
sourceIsEphemeral?: boolean,
squash?: boolean,
strategy?: "merge" | "ff_only" | "ff_prefer", // default: "ff_prefer"
targetBranch: string, // minLength: 1
targetIsEphemeral?: boolean,
},
spaceId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Edit, approve, decline, or unlist an entry. Read its current revision first. Every action advances the revision; use the returned revision for the next action. Approval publishes the reviewed working copy after checking live public access again. Supply versionId from the live version you reviewed. Use approval to restore an unlisted entry. Withdrawn entries require a new creator submission. The live version must still match versionId at approval. Approval records that version as a baseline. Later publishes change the destination content without hiding the listing. Requires current membership of the Show & Tell team.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__moderateShowAndTellEntry(args: {
body:
 | {
action: "edit",
category?: ("apps" | "games" | "art" | "stories" | "personal") | null,
// A curated gallery image on the Spacefast website, used instead of the automatic screenshot. null goes back to the screenshot.
coverUrl?:
 | string // maxLength: 2048, format: "uri"
 | null
,
credit?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 80
description?: string, // maxLength: 280
id: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 64
revision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
// maxItems: 10
tags?: Array<
string // minLength: 1, maxLength: 40
>,
title?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 255
}
 | {
action: "approve",
id: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 64
revision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
versionId: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 64
}
 | {
action: "decline",
creatorReason: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 1000
id: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 64
internalNote?: string, // maxLength: 2000
revision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
}
 | {
action: "unlist",
id: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 64
revision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
}
,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Use this tool when publish returns status publishing.
Pass job.poll.url as url when present. Otherwise, pass job.poll.operationId as operationId.
If done is false, wait retryAfter seconds before calling again.
Stop when result.done is true.
Report success only when result.status is succeeded.
For an archive build, inspect result.receipt.activation. Only activated confirms that this version is live.
If result.status is skipped, report that the build did not run.
For deployment or build status, call show_space_deployments with top-level space for an owned Space.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__operation_status(args: {
// Exact publish.result.job.poll.operationId.
operationId?: string, // minLength: 1
// Exact publish.result.job.poll.url. Prefer this field when present.
url?: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Select this domain as primary, restore the managed default hostname, answer this hostname with a whole-host redirect, or pass `hostname` to swap which half of an apex/www pair serves the Space.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__patchSpaceCustomDomain(args: {
body?: {
// Which of this attachment's two hostnames serves the Space. Accepts the apex or its `www` twin; the other one answers a 308 to it. Any other hostname is refused. For a legacy pair stored as separate rows, explicitly choosing a hostname configures both rows and returns the selected hostname's domain identity; existing routing is unchanged until this choice is made.
hostname?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 253
// Set or clear this hostname as the Space's primary URL.
primary?: boolean,
// Answer this hostname with a whole-host redirect instead of serving the Space. Pass null to serve the Space again.
redirect?:
 | {
// HTTP redirect status. Defaults to 308.
status?: 301 | 302 | 307 | 308, // default: 308
// Redirect destination: an absolute URL, or a space (optionally with a path).
to:
 | {
// Absolute URL to redirect to.
url: string, // format: "uri"
}
 | {
// Path on the target space.
path?: string, // maxLength: 255
// Space to redirect to (`spc_...`).
spaceId: string, // minLength: 1
}
,
}
 | null
,
},
domainId: string,
spaceId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Applies a graph replacement patch against a known base revision for collaborative editing.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__patchSpaceTagRevisionGraph(args: {
body: {
baseGraphRevision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 1
operations: Array<
{
op: "replace",
path: "graph",
// Tag graph v1 write input. The server enforces these limits: 262144 encoded bytes, 256 tags, 256 triggers, 256 variables, and 64 system modules. The server also enforces 256 items per nested array, 64 keys per object, 65536 encoded bytes per string, and 16 nested levels. Unknown top-level fields are rejected.
value: {
consentPolicy?: { [key: string]: any },
format?: "spacefast.tag_graph.v1", // default: "spacefast.tag_graph.v1"
systemModules?: { [key: string]: any },
tags?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
triggers?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
variables?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
},
}
>,
},
revisionId: string,
spaceId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Applies a graph replacement patch against a known base revision for collaborative team editing.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__patchTeamTagRevisionGraph(args: {
body: {
baseGraphRevision: integer, // maximum: 9007199254740991, exclusiveMinimum: 0
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 1
operations: Array<
{
op: "replace",
path: "graph",
// Tag graph v1 write input. The server enforces these limits: 262144 encoded bytes, 256 tags, 256 triggers, 256 variables, and 64 system modules. The server also enforces 256 items per nested array, 64 keys per object, 65536 encoded bytes per string, and 16 nested levels. Unknown top-level fields are rejected.
value: {
consentPolicy?: { [key: string]: any },
format?: "spacefast.tag_graph.v1", // default: "spacefast.tag_graph.v1"
systemModules?: { [key: string]: any },
tags?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
triggers?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
variables?: { [key: string]: any }[], // default: [], maxItems: 256
},
}
>,
},
revisionId: string,
teamId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Canonicalizes the hostname and returns an advisory hostability verdict. A negative verdict usually means the domain is already in use with another host — it can still be added and claimed with a TXT ownership proof, so treat the verdict as a warning, not a block.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__preflightDomain(args: {
// Apex or concrete hostname to preflight; canonicalized server-side.
name: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 253
// Team the domain would be added to. Defaults the same way `POST /v1/domains` does.
teamId?: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Apply the inverse of a non-merge commit to working files. Resolve conflicts explicitly. Keep staging and saved history unchanged.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__prepareSpaceSourceWorkspaceUndo(args: {
body: {
// Revision from the last workspace response. Read the workspace again after a revision conflict.
expectedRevision: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
// Unique ID for this operation. Reuse this ID and the same input after an uncertain response.
operationId: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 128
// Non-merge source commit to undo in working files. This does not commit or deploy.
sourceCommitSha: string, // pattern: /^[a-f0-9]{40}$/
},
spaceId: string,
workspaceId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Promotes a ready version to a channel (`live` by default). Rolling back to an earlier version creates a new version from its original files with current rewrites by default. Set `refreshRewrites=false` to activate the saved version exactly. Dynamic platform features stay current in either mode. Waits for completion by default. Pass `async=1` to get an operation handle to poll instead. When refreshing, wait for the returned `data.id`, which differs from the selected version.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__promoteSpaceVersion(args: {
Idempotency-Key?: string, // maxLength: 255
// Promote in the background and return the operation handle instead of waiting (true/1).
async?: "0" | "1" | "true" | "false",
body?: {
// Channel to point at this version. Defaults to "live". Non-live channel names are rejected with `channel_unsupported` until additional channels ship.
channel?: string, // minLength: 1
// When rolling back, refresh HTML rewrites from the selected version's original files using current settings and create a new version. Defaults to true. Set false to restore the saved version exactly. Dynamic Spacefast features stay current.
refreshRewrites?: boolean,
},
// Content-Type for the request body. Declared media types for this operation, in spec order.
contentType?: "application/json" | "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" | "multipart/form-data", // default: "application/json"
spaceId: string,
versionId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Publish inline files or completed uploads to Spacefast. This hosted tool requires a signed-in connection. It cannot publish anonymously or read local filesystem paths.
Before building or changing a Space for a signed-in user, call `getAccount`, then `getTeamAgentContext` for that team. Apply the design system and skills it returns, and say in one line whose design system you will use, or that the team has none. Get each brand file the page needs with `getTeamDesignSystemAsset` and publish a copy with the page: its URL is private, so visitors can't load it.
Set public access only when the user explicitly requests public access.
Set files for a small artifact, or uploadId for a completed durable upload. Uploaded files require sign-in.
Sell requires sign-in and a team-owned Space. Include sf.jsonc, product JSON and paid files; paid files stay private.
To edit files in an existing Space, use the source workspace operations.
With spaceId, this publishes a complete new version of that Space and replaces its files; do it only when the user asks to overwrite that Space.
Set a new requestId before the first authenticated call. Reuse it only to retry the same input after a timeout.
If status is publishing, use the operation_status continuation in result.job.poll.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__publish(args: {
// Set initial access when this publish creates a team-owned Space: private admits the owning team, public admits anyone on the web. Omit it to use the team's default. Do not set this field when you update a Space. Set public only when the user explicitly asks for public access.
access?: "private" | "public",
// Optional changelog for this publish version. Set it only if the user supplied a changelog. This field does not change the Space description.
description?: string, // maxLength: 2000
// Complete files for a small artifact, or provide uploadId. For existing Space file edits, use the source workspace API.
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 1000
files?: Array<
{
// File data. Use plain text for utf8. Use base64 text for base64 encoding.
content: string,
// Encoding of content. Default: utf8. Use base64 for binary files.
encoding?: "utf8" | "base64", // default: "utf8"
// Relative path of this published file. Do not use an absolute path.
path: string, // minLength: 1
}
>,
// For an authenticated publish, set one unique value before the first call. Reuse the same value only when you retry that call after a timeout.
requestId?: string, // minLength: 16, maxLength: 200
// Optional slug for a new Space. Set it only if the user supplied a slug.
slug?: string, // minLength: 2, maxLength: 55
// Destination Space id for this publication. Omit this field to create a Space.
spaceId?: string, // minLength: 1
// For a new Space in a requested team, set the destination team id or slug. Authorization failures stop this publish. They do not create an anonymous Space.
teamId?: string, // minLength: 1
// Optional title for a new Space. Set it only if the user supplied a title.
title?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 255
// Completed durable upload ID from completeUpload. Requires sign-in. Use instead of files or path. Reuse it when retrying this publication.
uploadId?: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Buys up to 10 registrable apex domains as one purchase on the paying team's saved payment method. Quotes each, adds it to the team's inventory, and holds them all. With purchasing power (`billing:purchase` on the paying team) and `expectedTotalCents` equal to the live total before tax, the payment method is charged now, including without X-Spacefast-Client. Otherwise nothing is charged: `data.purchase.status` is `awaiting_confirmation` (or `awaiting_payment_method` with no usable payment method), and you give the user `data.purchase.confirmUrl`, or confirm it yourself with confirmTeamPurchase if you have purchasing power. One name that can't be bought refuses the whole cart. A different live total refuses with purchase_total_changed. A hostname the team already holds is registered on its existing record. Released Spacefast CLIs before 0.9.0, identified by their capabilities header without X-Spacefast-Cli-Version, are never charged from expectedTotalCents: the purchase is held for a person, and the receipt adds the `checkout` pay link those CLIs read.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__purchaseDomain(args: {
body: {
analytics?: {
anonymousId: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 128, pattern: /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/
path: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 2048, pattern: /^\/(?:[^/?#]+\/){0,2}domains(?:\/[^?#]*)?$/
sessionId: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
