Changes only the fields sent. `newSpaceGrantPreset` applies to future spaces only. `privateSpacesOnly` and `noindex` apply to every space the team owns: turning `privateSpacesOnly` on revokes every public Grant on them, turns `noindex` on, and changes a `public` new-space default to `private`. While it is on, a `public` default or `noindex: false` returns 409 `team_private_spaces_only`. Turning it off makes spaces whose sf.jsonc declares `access.public` public again; `publicSpaceCount` counts them. `privateSpacesOnly` and `noindex` change only from a dashboard browser session: API keys, CLI logins and OAuth or agent tokens get 403 `interactive_session_required`. The spaces' runtime update continues in the background. `restrictSpaceTransfer` is parent-controlled and available on Enterprise/Internal. Both enabling and disabling use standard sensitive-action confirmation for session callers; delegated bearer authority and scopes are unchanged. Subteams inherit the parent value and cannot override it. A mixed write is atomic. Incoming transfers and existing transfer permissions are unchanged. `blockShareLinks` sets the team's own share-link block (owners and admins): link Grants on its spaces stop admitting anyone but are kept, and new links return 409 `team_share_links_blocked`. A parent team's block binds every subteam, and a subteam turning it off gets 409 `share_link_policy_enforced_by_parent`. Turning it off from an agent connection returns 409 `confirmation_required` until a person approves; then send the same request with X-Spacefast-Continuation-Token. A credential that can't ask a person, such as a plain API key, gets 403 `authorization_level_not_allowed`.

```ts
mcp__Spacefast__setTeamAccessDefaults(args: {
X-Spacefast-Continuation-Token?: string, // maxLength: 4096
body?: {
// Set this team's own share-link block. Team owners and admins only. On a parent team it binds every subteam; a subteam can block on its own but cannot turn off its parent's block (409 `share_link_policy_enforced_by_parent`). Turning it off from an agent connection needs a person's approval: 409 `confirmation_required`, then send the same request with X-Spacefast-Continuation-Token. A credential that can't ask a person, such as a plain API key, can turn it on but gets 403 `authorization_level_not_allowed` turning it off. While `privateSpacesOnly` is true, turning it off returns 409 `team_private_spaces_only`.
blockShareLinks?: boolean,
// The general access new spaces start with: `private` (the whole team), `parent_team` (the team and everyone in its parent team, who can view and comment) or `public` (anyone on the web). `team` is accepted as a legacy spelling of `private`. `parent_team` needs a subteam on an Enterprise or Internal family: a root team returns 422 `parent_team_access_requires_subteam`, another family 403 `enterprise_required`.
newSpaceGrantPreset?: "private" | "team" | "parent_team" | "public",
// The general access new spaces start with in each subteam created from now on: `private` or `parent_team`. Existing subteams keep their own default. Root teams on Enterprise or Internal only: a subteam returns 422 `new_subteam_default_requires_root_team`, another plan 403 `enterprise_required`.
newSubteamSpaceGrantPreset?: "private" | "parent_team",
// When true, every space in this team serves platform noindex directives on its live hostnames, whatever its own `noindex` says, and a space cannot turn it off. Always true while `privateSpacesOnly` is true. Dashboard only: these rules guard against agents, so API keys, CLI logins and OAuth or agent tokens get 403 `interactive_session_required`; read them instead.
noindex?: boolean,
// When true, no space in this team can be public: public Grants, public new-space defaults, and `access: public` on create or publish are refused with `team_private_spaces_only`, and public access declared in sf.jsonc is ignored. Turning it on revokes every public Grant on the team's spaces, turns `noindex` on, and blocks the team's share links (`blockShareLinks`), which on a parent team binds every subteam. Dashboard only: these rules guard against agents, so API keys, CLI logins and OAuth or agent tokens get 403 `interactive_session_required`; read them instead.
privateSpacesOnly?: boolean,
// Restrict outgoing transfers to the parent team and its subteams. Only parent owners and admins on Enterprise or Internal may change it. Session callers use standard sensitive-action confirmation; delegated API/agent authority and scopes remain unchanged.
restrictSpaceTransfer?: boolean,
// Choose whether subteam transfer requests notify all destination admins or prefer directly assigned subteam admins with parent-admin fallback. Only the controlling parent team's owners/admins or delegated team-write credentials may change it. Subteams must change it on the parent team.
transferRequestNotificationAudience?: "all_admins" | "direct_admins_first",
// Choose who receives public/private change emails for this team and its subteams. Only the controlling parent team's owners and admins or delegated team-write credentials can change this. A subteam must change it on the parent team.
visibilityEmailAudience?: "admins" | "all_members",
},
teamId: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
