Changes settings of a domain the team registered through Spacefast: `transferLock: true` (relocks at the registrar and remains available with transfers disabled; send it on its own, with no other setting; unlock with the `transfer_out` registration action), WHOIS `privacySetting`, the registrant (`contactId` of a saved contact), and the `autoRenew` preference. Privacy and registrant changes reach the registrar first and are saved only once it accepts: a refusal answers 409 (`domain_transfer_locked`, `domain_registrar_disputed` or `domain_registrar_inactive`) and changes nothing, and an unconfirmed write answers 503 `domain_registration_unconfirmed`; send the same change again. A new registrant starts the registry's 60-day transfer lock. Editing a saved contact updates every registration using it at the registrar. A domain belongs to the person whose contact it is registered to: only they move it to another contact, and only to one of their own. Unlocking transfers, turning off privacy, or changing the registrant affects who controls the domain and whose details are public, so make those changes only at the user's request. `autoRenew` is on for every registration unless its owner turns it off. While on, Spacefast notifies the team's owners and admins in the dashboard's Notifications 60 days before expiry (no email), then renews the domain for a year from its current expiry, charging the paying team's saved payment method from 30 days before it expires and retrying until it does; nothing is tried once it has expired. A name the team first hears about inside 37 days (turned on, bought or transferred in late) is charged no sooner than a week after that notice; `autoRenewChargesFrom` on the registration gives the earliest charge, or null when auto-renew can't renew this term. A term nobody was told about is never charged: a paying team with no owner or admin is not charged, and `autoRenewChargesFrom` is null until it has one, who is then told and charged no sooner than a week later. Turning it off releases any automatic renewal not yet charged. A missing payment method or a declined charge can still stop it. A person can still renew it early with the `renew` registration action.

