Send `expectedRevision` (409 `space_share_changed` when stale, with the current Share). General access takes one of three modes: `level` (`private`, `parent_team`, `public` with `role`), the independent `public`/`parentTeam` switches, or `closeAllPublic: true` to close public access while keeping parent-team access as set. Turning public off removes every public rule this API can change, path rules included. `effect.stillPublic` and `effective.anonymous` report remaining access. `closeAllPublic: true` answers 409 `space_access_narrowing_blocked` if a public rule this API can't change would keep anything open. Going public never removes parent-team access. `comments.previews`/`comments.live` take `default`, `on` or `off` (Live needs Previews: 422 `comments_live_requires_previews`). Answers `data: { share, effect }`: Share as it now reads and what the change did. `dryRun: true` returns them and changes nothing. From the Space bar or an agent connection, a change that adds a way in answers 409 `confirmation_required` until the person confirms it at `url`; then send the same request with X-Spacefast-Continuation-Token.

```ts
