Read benchmark results and published model comparisons from Tamarind Benchmarks.

For questions about Tamarind's benchmark scores or data, discover the public id with
listBenchmarks(scope="public"), then call this tool. No prediction or evaluation is launched.
Public ids read existing published data; native ids read the caller's custom benchmark results.

Public results declare source=hosted and resultSchema. statistics keeps the published leaderboard,
units and denominators; items keep interface or POISK binder/decoy pair scores. No new computation runs.
Public task/subset/target filters apply only to hosted data. Start with limit=0 for the statistics.

json returns {statistics, items, next}: statistics ranks each model on each metric (value, n,
rank, coverage; a benchmark without models has values at the top level) and comes on every
page; items are one per row with each model's cell status and values (design models nest
their designs). Start with limit=0 for the leaderboard alone. csv returns {"csv": text}, one
line per (row, model[, design]); per-model statistics are only in json.
Native resultSchema defines metric sources and distinguishes stored properties from computed
metrics. JSON comparisons carry reference/prediction values and their exact source properties/jobs.
CSV includes resultSchema; a leading apostrophe on text is spreadsheet formula escaping.

For native custom benchmarks, models are compared only on rows every one of them has a value for (`n`, `comparedRows`), so
while one model's cells are still running a statistic can be null for every model: wait until
