Submit ONE job for protein analysis using one of the available tools.

Submits the settings you construct to the Tamarind API
(POST https://app.tamarind.bio/api/submit-job). Requests only ever go
to the Tamarind platform; the endpoint is fixed and not caller-controlled.

Protein Solubilization uses the native Jobs API. Its response contains
one pipeline run per results entry: check handoff="accepted", retain Id,
and use getPipelineRun/getPipelineRunResults/stopPipelineRun. For an
unconfirmed handoff, retry the unchanged request with the same submitId.

Running a FINETUNED model (inference) is a normal submitJob — there is no
separate endpoint. Call listFinetunedModels, pick a model whose `status`
is "Available", submit its `inferenceType` as `type`, and pass its `id`
as the top-level `modelId` (not inside `settings`). `settings` are the
inference tool's own inputs: getJobSchema(jobType="<inferenceType>").
Example: {"jobName": "my-predictions", "type": "chemprop-inference",
"modelId": "<id>", "settings": {"smiles": ["CCO"]}}.

Training / finetuning a model (e.g. chemprop-finetune, esmc-finetune,
nos, proteus): prefer submitFinetuningRun, with `model` set to the
finetune tool name. A finetune tool sent here still goes through — if
the platform answers that it belongs on its finetune endpoint (code
"use_finetune_endpoint"), the connector resends it to POST /finetune
once, automatically.

IMPORTANT: Use this only for a single job. If you are about to submit
more than one job (e.g. folding several sequences, scanning variants,
or chaining a design job's output into structure prediction), call
submitBatch ONCE instead of calling submitJob in a loop. Looping
submitJob is slower, ungroupable, and rate-limited. For ProteinMPNN ->
AlphaFold/Chai, read the design job's results (listJobFiles /
getJobFile), choose the sequences, and pass them to submitBatch as
`settings` or as a fasta/csv via `fromFile`.



**Responses:**

- **200** (Success): Job submitted successfully

- **400**: Bad request - invalid parameters

- **401**: Unauthorized - invalid API key

- **429**: Too many requests - rate limit exceeded

```ts
mcp__Tamarind_Bio__submitJob(args: {
// Protein Solubilization prepared pickerComplex references with complexId and groupId; omit settings.pdbFile when supplied.
inputs?: { [key: string]: any }[],
// Unique name for the job
jobName: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 100, pattern: /^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/
// OPTIONAL. Run inference with a FINETUNED model: the model's `id` from
// listFinetunedModels. A TOP-LEVEL field, not a setting. `type` must be
// the model's `inferenceType` (any other is refused); the model must be
// `Available` and one you can access (yours, or a teammate's shared with
// your organization). Preferred over `modelName` — names are not unique, and
// when both are sent `modelId` wins.
modelId?: string, // minLength: 1
// OPTIONAL. Run inference with a finetuned model by its `name` from
// listFinetunedModels, when you do not have its `id`. A name always means
// YOUR model when you own one by that name, so use `modelId` for a
// teammate's. Most inference tools need one of `modelId`/`modelName`.
modelName?: string, // minLength: 1
// OPTIONAL organization project to file this job under — its project id
// OR its name. A TOP-LEVEL field; it is not a setting, so do not put it
// in `settings`.
//
// REQUIRED for organizations that have turned on "require a project
// tag". Those accounts reject an untagged submission with HTTP 400, and
// a PERSONAL project does not satisfy the policy. You do not have to
// look one up first: that 400 body carries `availableProjects`, the
// projects this account may use — retry with one of their `id` or
// `name` values. If more than one could fit, ask the user which rather
// than choosing for them.
//
// Send a real value or omit the field — `""` is NOT "no tag": the backend
// reads it as omitted, so an org that requires one refuses the submission
// all over again while the connector looks like it accepted your tag.
projectTag?: string, // minLength: 1, pattern: /\S/
// Job-specific settings. Structure depends on job type.
//
// IMPORTANT: Use the getJobSchema tool to get the exact parameter schema for your job type.
// Example: getJobSchema(jobType="proteinmpnn") returns the detailed schema with all parameters.
//
// Documentation: https://app.tamarind.bio/api-docs
settings: { [key: string]: any },
// Protein Solubilization requires a new UUID per intentional submission. Retry with the same submitId and unchanged request.
submitId?: string,
// Tool to use for the job.
//
// IMPORTANT: Use getAvailableTools() to discover available tools dynamically.
// Tool list is updated frequently - do not rely on hardcoded values.
//
// Example workflow:
// 1. Call getAvailableTools(search="alphafold") to find tools
// 2. Call getJobSchema(jobType="alphafold") to get parameter schema
// 3. Call submitJob with the tool name and settings
type: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

